    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "{\"analysis\":\"Only iso_3.15 has been measured. It uses almost the whole bit budget, so a layer upgrade needs a matching downgrade or a cheaper format. At their current bit width, the layers where the loss concentrates already use the method with the lowest measured KL. That leaves two kinds of move. The first is option tuning that does not change the bit count (act_order, damp). The second frees bits by switching rht_gptq_int3 to weight.group_size=256, which roughly halves the stored scale overhead. The freed bits pay for upgrading model.layers.14.mlp.down_proj from rht_gptq_int2 to rht_gptq_int3 and model.layers.27.mlp.gate_proj from rht_gptq_int3 to rht_gptq_int4. Last round's proposals were all refused because their rationale used a rounded KL value, so these rationales use only exact numbers from the cited records.\",\"stop\":false,\"proposals\":[{\"name\":\"iso_actorder\",\"base\":\"iso_3.15\",\"changes\":[],\"options\":{\"gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"rht_gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"rht_gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"rht_gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true}},\"rationale\":\"Uses the same bits as base iso_3.15 [E514ab09c524e]. Setting weight_algo.act_order=true makes GPTQ quantize the columns with the largest activations first. That should help layers with heavy-tailed activations, such as model.layers.27.mlp.up_proj, whose activation kurtosis is 1090.09 [E24beed188b6a] and whose gptq_int3 KL is 0.0057182 [Ef04d8aa7bded].\",\"cites\":[\"E514ab09c524e\",\"E24beed188b6a\",\"Ef04d8aa7bded\"]},{\"name\":\"g256_rht3_upgrade_l14down_l27gate\",\"base\":\"iso_3.15\",\"changes\":[{\"block\":14,\"kind\":\"down_proj\",\"method\":\"rht_gptq_int3\"},{\"block\":27,\"kind\":\"gate_proj\",\"method\":\"rht_gptq_int4\"}],\"options\":{\"rht_gptq_int3\":{\"weight.group_size\":256}},\"rationale\":\"Setting weight.group_size=256 for rht_gptq_int3 roughly halves its scale overhead, and the freed bits pay for two upgrades. model.layers.14.mlp.down_proj moves from rht_gptq_int2 (KL 0.00633466 [E4c3f9b73e065]) to rht_gptq_int3 (KL 0.00181478 [E90bd4b2f3645]). model.layers.27.mlp.gate_proj moves from rht_gptq_int3 (KL 0.00498703 [Efa0bb391da67]) to rht_gptq_int4 (KL 0.00153131 [Ef428ac081334]). Base is [E514ab09c524e].\",\"cites\":[\"E514ab09c524e\",\"E4c3f9b73e065\",\"E90bd4b2f3645\",\"Efa0bb391da67\",\"Ef428ac081334\"]},{\"name\":\"iso_damp_high\",\"base\":\"iso_3.15\",\"changes\":[],\"options\":{\"gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05},\"gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05},\"gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05},\"rht_gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05},\"rht_gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05},\"rht_gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05}},\"rationale\":\"Uses the same bits as base [E514ab09c524e]. Raising damp to weight_algo.damp=0.05 regularizes the Hessian, which may stop GPTQ from overfitting the calibration windows at 2 and 3 bits. The base's measured validation KL is above its predicted value [E514ab09c524e]. Overfitting would also explain why model.layers.14.mlp.down_proj under rht_gptq_int2 has KL 0.00633466 [E4c3f9b73e065].\",\"cites\":[\"E514ab09c524e\",\"E4c3f9b73e065\"]}]}",
    "structured_output": {
     "analysis": "Only iso_3.15 has been measured. It uses almost the whole bit budget, so a layer upgrade needs a matching downgrade or a cheaper format. At their current bit width, the layers where the loss concentrates already use the method with the lowest measured KL. That leaves two kinds of move. The first is option tuning that does not change the bit count (act_order, damp). The second frees bits by switching rht_gptq_int3 to weight.group_size=256, which roughly halves the stored scale overhead. The freed bits pay for upgrading model.layers.14.mlp.down_proj from rht_gptq_int2 to rht_gptq_int3 and model.layers.27.mlp.gate_proj from rht_gptq_int3 to rht_gptq_int4. Last round's proposals were all refused because their rationale used a rounded KL value, so these rationales use only exact numbers from the cited records.",
